#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192654 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192585 :question/id #uuid "c700cc22-203a-5ad3-913c-e5eb507e22e3" :question/math-academy-id "e-13995" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}a+4b=1 \\\\ 2a+b=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $a$ from this system by filling in the missing information below.\n\n$\\qquad$ *To eliminate $a,$ multiply the $\\,\\textbf{__________}\\,$equation by $\\,\\textbf{______}\\,$, \nand add the equations.*" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $a$ in the first equation is $1,$ while in the second equation it is $2.$ \n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-2},$ then the coefficient of $a$ will turn into $-2,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $2$ in the second equation.\n\n![](images/2b/2b0aa0d1dbfeb1e711bde6e7741fe5706aa126d71c44ae417d3c78d01b83547a.svg)\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $a$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{-2a}-8b & =-2 \\\\ \\cancel{2a}+b & =-5 \\\\ (-8b+b) & =(-2-5) \\\\ -7b & =-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n*To eliminate $a,$ multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-2},$ and add the equations*."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93dcc73c-ce2d-5fa3-b32b-9fc600fb269e" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049060}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509241 :question-generator/id #uuid "b0954483-dbae-52d5-aa27-0d7a9746e93c" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186192654.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193241 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e0b7d00-1654-52b7-9052-7a91aba67a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.