"q-210859" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3s+4t=8 \\\\ s+5t=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $s$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $s,$ multiply the \n{{field-1}} \nequation by \n{{field-2}}, \nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $s$ in the first equation is $3,$ while in the second equation it is $1.$ \n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-3,$ then the coefficient of $s$ will turn into $-3,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $3$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3s+4t=8 \\\\ (\\,s+5t=10\\,)\\,\\times (-3)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}3s+4t=8 \\\\ -3s-15t=-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $s$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{3s}+4t & =8 \\\\ -\\cancel{3s}-15t & =-30 \\\\ (4t-15t) & =(8-30) \\\\ -11t & =-22 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n*Multiply the $\\text{second}$ equation by $-3,$ and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508917 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "396c0c6a-1e03-5316-868c-3693041a6a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508474} {:answer/id #uuid "7405e912-7fbf-5e14-9ed1-9fa8aad46b93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "396c0c6a-1e03-5316-868c-3693041a6a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508474} :answer-field/id #uuid "15d7b3eb-155c-54a4-84ac-4a02f7b9e7e6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508817} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "564482bf-2dea-55bc-82ec-61c16390e434" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508516} {:answer/id #uuid "802cf47d-d04d-59cb-9afb-86ba6294bc49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508578} {:answer/id #uuid "82dc65ea-5abd-5f0e-b1d6-8d53cd015c74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508583} {:answer/id #uuid "ed089b80-c77d-5a59-8fbf-99ba45caaf88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "564482bf-2dea-55bc-82ec-61c16390e434" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508516} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fa84268-830c-548e-ba16-e867f14c3bf3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508834}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2a68ca7c-dc16-5d70-b5c4-e7c98a96c8e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-238035" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}10x-3y=36 \\\\ 2x+5y=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $x$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $x,$ multiply the \n{{field-1}} \nequation by \n{{field-2}}, \nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $10,$ while in the second equation it is $2.$ \n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-5,$ then the coefficient of $x$ will turn into $-10,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $10$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}10x-3y=36 \\\\ (\\,2x+5y=-4\\,)\\,\\times (-5)\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}10x-3y=36 \\\\ -10x-25y=20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\cancel{10x}-3y & =36 \\\\ -\\cancel{10x}-25y & =20 \\\\ (-3y-25y) & =(36+20) \\\\ -28y & =56 \\\\ y & =-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n*Multiply the $\\text{second}$ equation by $-5,$ and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509133 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53ecbda6-7a57-5ced-b37b-67f3e0611d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509157} {:answer/id #uuid "5de6e3ad-5e74-5eaf-9366-87ca894f9566" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509165} {:answer/id #uuid "653a3e3d-63fb-5473-b192-2fbab82ed7c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509171} {:answer/id #uuid "b9ab6b5e-f7d5-5ac1-8e90-66c8945a033a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53ecbda6-7a57-5ced-b37b-67f3e0611d56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509157} :answer-field/id #uuid "55b88cc5-050d-5ed4-9161-b5ccd94b7ecc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509159} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71254510-dc0b-5ac5-8725-9ee4cc50d177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509180} {:answer/id #uuid "73f72834-ef24-5b1d-976b-7feaf1a9d939" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73f72834-ef24-5b1d-976b-7feaf1a9d939" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509181} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff3ef9d4-e8b8-5b98-a4cf-98c00e7da24b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "19893126-a14f-5669-bf14-122fe45ed903" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$\\{-2s - 5t = -4; s - t = 7$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $s$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $s$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $s$ in the first equation is $-2$, while in the second equation it is $1$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by ${\\color{blue}2}$, then the coefficient of $s$ will turn into $2$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-2$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\{-2s - 5t = -4; (s - t = 7)\\cdot (2)\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $s$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2s - 5t &= -4 \\\\\n2s - 2t &= 14 \\\\\n(-5t - 2t) &= (-4 + 14) \\\\\n-7t &= 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $s$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{second}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}2}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509137 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aeebf26-5c1d-5f04-804f-fdbb0e881867" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id