e first equation is $-1$, while in the second equation it is $5$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}5}$, then the coefficient of $u$ will turn into $-5$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $5$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{(-u + 7v = 0)\\cdot (5); 5u + 6v = -3\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $u$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5u + 35v &= 0 \\\\\n5u + 6v &= -3 \\\\\n(35v + 6v) &= (0 - 3) \\\\\n41v &= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $u$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}5}$, and add the equations*."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509185 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38a5e8cf-9679-5e37-af4f-2b17615357b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509148} {:answer/id #uuid "5f107f49-ca98-5c5c-ba01-7ed409d9584c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509167} {:answer/id #uuid "cab95ace-4eda-5db9-84f4-6e8b591ffd8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509209} {:answer/id #uuid "f64438e6-d808-5371-8b19-8ad9d9da997a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cab95ace-4eda-5db9-84f4-6e8b591ffd8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509209} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a877f6f-f677-54d3-8e13-f1e41a168341" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509196} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5508c343-1cde-52e2-b